    "breaking_changes": [
        "Every framework class renamed from App\\ to Frank\\. Any existing project referencing framework classes under App\\ (directly, or via an old single-folder install) will fatal on update.",
        "Project layout is now two sibling folders, framework/ and app/, instead of one. An existing pre-2.0.0 install cannot drop this release in place; it must be manually restructured into the split.",
        "EmailService::sendTenantOwnerAdvisory() renamed to sendPlatformOwnerSignupAlert(). Any caller using the old method name will fatal.",
        "EmailMessage's constructor no longer defaults from/fromName (previously defaulted to BitFitter's own address/name). Any caller constructing EmailMessage without passing them explicitly will now get a missing-argument error instead of a silent wrong sender.",
        "Container::singleton()/bind() and Router::add() now throw on a duplicate id/route instead of silently allowing the later registration to win. Any existing bootstrap.php that (even accidentally) registered the same id or route twice will now fatal on boot.",
        "POST /api/v1/tenant/{tenant_id}/organizations no longer exists as a live route by default — Api\\V1\\OrganizationController moved to app/Scaffold/examples/organization/ as a reference implementation, not live code.",
        "cron_task_reminders.php removed entirely. Any cron job pointing at this file will fail (the feature was already non-functional — referenced a non-existent Task model — so this removes dead weight rather than working functionality)."
    ],
    "ai_notes": [
        "The raw added/changed/removed file counts in this manifest are misleading on their own: this script only diffs framework/, and the 1.4.0 snapshot predates the framework/app split, when Views/, public/, Config/config.php, .env, and MYAPP.md all lived inside framework/ too. Most of the 65 'removed' files were moved to app/, not deleted — cross-check against app/ before treating anything here as a real loss.",
        "Similarly, most of the 16 'removed' routes are the same route re-added with a corrected Frank\\ handler string (previously an inconsistent mix of bare shorthand and wrong App\\ prefixes), or moved into app/bootstrap.php, which this framework-scoped script cannot see (e.g. the dashboard routes). The one route that is a genuine removal is the Organizations API endpoint — see breaking_changes.",
        "TenantOwnerAdvisoryTemplate.php / schema.sql appearing in 'removed' and PlatformOwnerSignupAlertTemplate.php / schema.core.sql appearing in 'added' are renames, not independent add/remove pairs.",
        "The full narrative version of this entry is in CHANGELOG.md under [2.0.0] — this manifest is the mechanical backing data it was written from."
    ],
